# EdgeConBCE

EdgeConBCE is a reproducible benchmark workspace for studying local/edge routing trade-offs in conformational B-cell epitope prediction on the DTU `BP3C50ID` benchmark family.

The repository started from the ideas in `DeepBCE.pdf` and now includes:

- a packaged benchmark pipeline under [`src/edgeconbce`](src/edgeconbce)
- real-data BP3 benchmarking with config-driven execution
- a modern PLM/contact extension on top of the heuristic baseline family
- 10-seed repeated evaluation with bootstrap intervals and paired sign tests
- scenario analysis, manuscript tables, baseline comparison, transport benchmarking, and figure-input generation

## Current Status

As of `2026-05-26`, the repository is `manuscript-drafting ready` for a benchmark/trade-off paper, but it is **not yet a strong SCI-grade methods result**.

What is complete:

- official DTU benchmark inputs are present:
  - [`BP3C50ID_training_set.fasta`](BP3C50ID_training_set.fasta)
  - [`BP3C50ID_external_test_set.fasta`](BP3C50ID_external_test_set.fasta)
- the real benchmark path is wrapped by the package entrypoint in [`src/edgeconbce/pipeline/run.py`](src/edgeconbce/pipeline/run.py)
- heuristic and modern policy families are both implemented
- 10-seed repeated BP3 evaluation is complete in [`outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci`](outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci)
- scenario analysis, paper tables, baseline comparison, transport benchmark, and figure inputs are generated
- unit-test coverage is in place under [`tests`](tests), with `22` passing tests in the current environment

What is still missing for a stronger publication claim:

- no local rerun of the official `BepiPred-3.0` executable or service outputs
- no second benchmark family beyond `BP3C50ID`
- carbon is still mostly estimated from fixed power assumptions rather than meter-based measurements
- transport benchmarking is localhost loopback, not a real remote two-node deployment
- the best repeated local results still do not convincingly exceed published `BepiPred-3.0` values

## Policy Families

Heuristic family:

- `local_only`
- `edge_only`
- `adaptive_split`
- `adaptive_carbon_guard`

Modern PLM/contact family:

- `plm_local_only`
- `plm_edge_only`
- `plm_adaptive_split`
- `plm_adaptive_conformal_guard`

## Latest Repeated Results

Source: [`outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci/bp3_real_multiseed_sci_summary.md`](outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci/bp3_real_multiseed_sci_summary.md)

10-seed aggregate over seeds `42` to `51`:

| policy | MCC | F1 | ROC AUC | latency ms | total gCO2e | raw share |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `local_only` | `0.1714` | `0.3553` | `0.6614` | `1.10` | `0.1200` | `0.0000` |
| `edge_only` | `0.2151` | `0.3873` | `0.6821` | `87.02` | `0.1406` | `1.0000` |
| `adaptive_split` | `0.2055` | `0.3819` | `0.6770` | `27.76` | `0.1604` | `0.2867` |
| `adaptive_carbon_guard` | `0.1727` | `0.3599` | `0.6604` | `13.40` | `0.1388` | `0.1333` |
| `plm_local_only` | `0.2061` | `0.3885` | `0.6829` | `111.10` | `0.1207` | `0.0000` |
| `plm_edge_only` | `0.2186` | `0.3986` | `0.6961` | `208.64` | `0.1441` | `1.0000` |
| `plm_adaptive_split` | `0.2104` | `0.3937` | `0.6857` | `164.01` | `0.1628` | `0.2933` |
| `plm_adaptive_conformal_guard` | `0.2104` | `0.3937` | `0.6857` | `164.01` | `0.1628` | `0.2933` |

Key repeated findings:

- `adaptive_split` materially improves quality over `local_only`, but it is worse than `edge_only` on total carbon
- `adaptive_carbon_guard` reduces routing and carbon relative to `adaptive_split`, but gives back most of the quality gain
- `plm_local_only` is a real quality upgrade over the heuristic local baseline without raw-sequence sharing
- `plm_edge_only` is the best repeated quality point in this repository, but it is also the slowest and shares every sequence
- `plm_adaptive_split` and `plm_adaptive_conformal_guard` do not yet show a decisive quality gain over `plm_local_only`
- `plm_adaptive_conformal_guard` currently collapses to the same operating point as `plm_adaptive_split`

## Baseline Position

Source: [`outputs/baseline_comparison_sci/baseline_comparison.md`](outputs/baseline_comparison_sci/baseline_comparison.md)

Published same-split `BepiPred-3.0` comparators remain the main reality check:

| model | ROC AUC | MCC | F1 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `plm_edge_only` | `0.6961` | `0.2186` | `0.3986` |
| `BepiPred-3.0 FFNN (ESM-1b)` | `0.6970` | `0.2200` | `0.4010` |
| `BepiPred-3.0 final FFNN (+ SeqLen)` | `0.7140` | `0.2410` | `n/a` |

Interpretation:

- the repository now has a credible modern local baseline and a contact-aware edge refinement path
- the best repeated result is close to published `BepiPred-3.0`, but does **not** clearly beat it
- this supports a benchmark/workflow paper better than a strong new-biology or state-of-the-art claim

