## How To Run

The package is laid out under `src/`, so the simplest repo-local workflow is:

```powershell
$env:PYTHONPATH="src"
```

Run the current real BP3 benchmark:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.run --config configs/bp3_real_v3.yaml
```

Run the 10-seed repeated BP3 evaluation:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.run --config configs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci.yaml
```

Generate manuscript tables:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.paper_tables `
  --repeated-results outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci/bp3_real_multiseed_sci_aggregate_results.json `
  --real-results outputs/edgeconbce_bp3_real_results_v3.json `
  --output-dir outputs/paper_tables_sci
```

Generate scenario analysis:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.scenario_analysis `
  --repeated-results outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci/bp3_real_multiseed_sci_aggregate_results.json `
  --output-dir outputs/scenario_analysis_sci
```

Generate baseline comparison:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.baseline_comparison `
  --repeated-results outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci/bp3_real_multiseed_sci_aggregate_results.json `
  --output-dir outputs/baseline_comparison_sci
```

Run the loopback transport benchmark:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.transport_benchmark `
  --real-results outputs/edgeconbce_bp3_real_results_v3.json `
  --output-dir outputs/transport_benchmark_sci
```

Generate figure-ready CSV inputs:

```powershell
python -m edgeconbce.pipeline.figure_inputs `
  --repeated-results outputs/bp3_repeated_eval_sci/bp3_real_multiseed_sci_aggregate_results.json `
  --real-results outputs/edgeconbce_bp3_real_results_v3.json `
  --baseline-results outputs/baseline_comparison_sci/baseline_comparison.json `
  --transport-results outputs/transport_benchmark_sci/transport_benchmark.json `
  --output-dir outputs/figure_inputs_sci
```

Run the test suite:

```powershell
python -m unittest discover -s tests -q
```

## Practical Notes

- the real-data BP3 path is still wrapped around the legacy runner in [`edgeconbce_real_benchmark_v2.py`](edgeconbce_real_benchmark_v2.py) through [`src/edgeconbce/pipeline/real_benchmark.py`](src/edgeconbce/pipeline/real_benchmark.py)
- the modern PLM/contact extension expects local ESM checkpoint files under `.torchcache/hub/checkpoints/`
- repeated-run summaries report bootstrap confidence intervals and paired sign tests
- transport benchmarking currently measures localhost serialized payloads, not a WAN or real edge node

## Current Claim Boundary

What this repository can support today:

- a reproducible local-edge BCE benchmark workflow
- a PLM-based local screening baseline with contact-aware edge refinement
- repeated-run latency/carbon/privacy trade-off analysis on `BP3C50ID`

What it should **not** claim yet:

- state of the art
- biological superiority over modern BCE predictors
- greener-than-all-baselines deployment
- realistic deployment carbon savings from end-to-end measured infrastructure

